      <section>
        <h2 class="mb-2 text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider" style="color:var(--jfo-accent);font-family:ui-monospace,monospace"><span data-i18n="homeWhatTitle">What Is a JSON Formatter Online?</span></h2>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed" style="color:var(--jfo-text-2)">
          <span data-i18n-html="homeWhatBody1">A <strong style="color:var(--jfo-text-1)">JSON formatter online</strong> — also known as a JSON beautifier or <strong style="color:var(--jfo-text-1)">pretty JSON formatter</strong> — is a browser-based tool that takes raw, compact, or minified JSON text and restructures it with consistent indentation, proper line breaks, and aligned key–value pairs. The result is clean, human-readable JSON that makes debugging API responses, configuration files, and data payloads dramatically faster and easier.</span>
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed" style="color:var(--jfo-text-2)">
          <span data-i18n-html="homeWhatBody2">Developers who work with REST APIs and GraphQL endpoints regularly receive responses as a single dense line of text. Dropping that blob into this <strong style="color:var(--jfo-text-1)">free JSON formatter</strong> instantly transforms it into a structured, indented document — revealing the exact shape of the data so every key and value is visible at a glance. No copying into an IDE, no installing browser plugins, no switching tools.</span>
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="mb-2 text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider" style="color:var(--jfo-accent);font-family:ui-monospace,monospace"><span data-i18n="homeHowTitle">How to Use This Free Online JSON Formatter</span></h2>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed" style="color:var(--jfo-text-2)">
          <span data-i18n-html="homeHowBody1">Using this <strong style="color:var(--jfo-text-1)">free online JSON formatter</strong> takes three seconds. Paste your JSON into the left editor panel, choose your indentation style — 2 spaces, 4 spaces, or tab — then click <strong style="color:var(--jfo-text-1)">⚡ Format</strong>. The right panel instantly displays syntax-highlighted, beautifully indented output. Copy it to the clipboard, download it as a <code style="font-family:ui-monospace,monospace;font-size:0.85em;color:var(--jfo-accent)">.json</code> file, or load a file directly from disk. Your input is automatically saved in the browser — switching to the Validator or Minifier tab and back restores exactly what you had.</span>
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed" style="color:var(--jfo-text-2)">
          <span data-i18n-html="homeHowBody2">The <strong style="color:var(--jfo-text-1)">JSON formatter tool</strong> does not auto-format on every keystroke. It waits for your explicit click so you stay in control — paste, edit, then format when you are ready. An amber pulse dot on the Format button signals that your input has changed since the last format, so you always know the output is fresh.</span>
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="mb-2 text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider" style="color:var(--jfo-accent);font-family:ui-monospace,monospace"><span data-i18n="homeValidatorTitle">JSON Formatter and Validator — Both in One Tool</span></h2>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed" style="color:var(--jfo-text-2)">
          <span data-i18n-html="homeValidatorBody1">This is more than a <strong style="color:var(--jfo-text-1)">pretty JSON formatter</strong> — it is a full <strong style="color:var(--jfo-text-1)">JSON formatter and validator</strong> combined. Every time you click Format, your JSON is silently validated against RFC 8259. If there is a syntax error — a missing comma, an unquoted key, a trailing comma after the last item, or mismatched brackets — a red error bar appears with the exact line and column of the problem. You get a precise location, not a vague "invalid JSON" message.</span>
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed" style="color:var(--jfo-text-2)">
          <span data-i18n-html="homeValidatorBody2">This makes the tool a dual-purpose <strong style="color:var(--jfo-text-1)">JSON formatter &amp; validator</strong>: format successfully and you have proof the JSON is valid; fail to format and you have the exact coordinates of the error. For deeper analysis — total key counts, maximum nesting depth, and per-error structural context — use the dedicated <a href="/json-validator" style="color:var(--jfo-accent);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:2px">JSON Validator</a>.</span>
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="mb-2 text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider" style="color:var(--jfo-accent);font-family:ui-monospace,monospace"><span data-i18n="homeWhyTitle">Why This Is the Best JSON Formatter Online</span></h2>
        <div class="grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-3">
          <div class="rounded-lg border p-3" style="border-color:var(--jfo-border);background:var(--jfo-bg-soft)">
            <div data-i18n="homeWhyFreeTitle" class="mb-1 text-xs font-semibold" style="color:var(--jfo-text-1)">100% Free, Forever</div>
            <p data-i18n-html="homeWhyFreeBody" class="text-xs leading-relaxed" style="color:var(--jfo-text-3)">No sign-up, no rate limits, no paywalled features. Every tool on this site is completely free — the <strong>best free JSON formatter</strong> available with zero strings attached.</p>
          </div>
